ute care hospitals offer medical and surgical services, including inpatient care, intensive care, cardiac care, diagnostic services, and emergency services; and outpatient services, such as outpatient surgery, laboratory, radiology, respiratory therapy, cardiology, and physical therapy. The company was formerly known as HCA Holdings, Inc. HCA Healthcare, Inc. was founded in 1968 and is headquartered in Nashville, Tennessee.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Samuel N. Hazen | CEO & Director | Age 65 | Compensation: $7.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 230K people. Revenue per employee of $329K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 7%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $33K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 23\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["HCA Healthcare, Inc. is a large-cap healthcare business with a $104.2B market cap on $75.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 25% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 17-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $7.7B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.86\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 5.4\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 10.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 17% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 1.8\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $5.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 16% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 35% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 35% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Healthcare peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term 